== usage head
sat_runner: Usage: see flags.
This program solves a given problem with the CP-SAT solver.

  Flags from root/or-tools/ortools/sat/sat_runner.cc:
    --competition_mode (If true, output the log in a competition format.);
      default: false;
    --domain_file (Protobuf file containing a CpModelResponse. If present, the
      tightened models will be used to reduce the domain of variables.);
      default: "";
    --fingerprint_intermediate_solutions (Attach the fingerprint of intermediate
      solutions to the output.); default: false;
    --force_interleave_search (If true, enable interleaved workers when
      num_workers is 1.); default: false;
    --hint_file (Protobuf file containing a CpModelResponse. The solution will
      be used as a hint to bootstrap the search.); default: "";
    --input (Required: input file of the problem to solve. Many format are
      supported:.cnf (sat, max-sat, weighted max-sat), .opb (pseudo-boolean
      sat/optim) and by default the CpModelProto proto (binary or text).);
      default: "";
    --output (If non-empty, write the response there. By default it uses the
      binary format except if the file extension is '.txt'.); default: "";
    --params (Parameters for the sat solver in a text format of the
      SatParameters proto, example: --params=use_conflicts:true.); default: "";
    --wcnf_use_strong_slack (If true, when we add a slack variable to reify a
      soft clause, we enforce the fact that when it is true, the clause must be
      false.); default: true;

Try --helpfull to get a list of all flags or --help=substring shows help for
flags which include specified substring in either in the name, or description or
path.
